  "description": "Shenora's Android shell: the MAUI HybridWebView IPC transport (the same envelope the desktop shell speaks, over SendRawMessage/RawMessageReceived), the resource interceptor that answers a page's byte ranges, a UI-thread dispatcher, safe-area insets, and the Android implementations of the Shenora shell contracts — native file dialogs, a MediaCodec-backed audio and video conversion pipeline with device capability probing, an ExoPlayer/MediaPlayer media player, and a MediaSession playback session for the lock screen and headphone controls. The platform owns the loop, so the app drives ShenoraApplication.Start/Stop from its own lifecycle rather than calling Run. Shares its source with Shenora.iOS.",
